# Every tracked text file is LF in the repository, and prettier requires LF.
# Check it out as LF on every platform too: a CRLF checkout (Git for
# Windows' core.autocrlf=true default) reaches the emitted C++ wherever a
# program observes its own source text -- Function.prototype.toString copies
# it verbatim, as node does -- so the same commit emitted different C++ on
# Windows, and prettier --check failed on every file there.
* text=auto eol=lf
